---
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const examples = [
  { id: 'subject', label: 'Sujet en premier' },
  { id: 'time', label: 'Temps en premier' },
  { id: 'object', label: 'Objet en premier' },
];

const sentenceTypes = [
  { label: 'Phrase affirmative', note: 'verbe en position 2', href: null },
  { label: 'Question', note: 'position 1 ou 2 selon le type', href: withBase('/theorie/syntaxe/les-questions/') },
  { label: 'Impératif', note: 'verbe au début', href: withBase('/theorie/conjugaison/imperatif/') },
  { label: 'Subordonnée', note: 'règle propre au connecteur', href: withBase('/theorie/syntaxe/') },
];

const sentenceGroups = [
  ['Verbe', 'la forme conjuguée'],
  ['Sujet', 'qui fait l’action'],
  ['CVD', 'qui ? quoi ?'],
  ['CVI', 'à qui ? à quoi ?'],
  ['Groupe prépositionnel', 'où ? quand ? avec qui ?'],
];
---

<section class="syntax-lesson verb-position-lesson" aria-labelledby="verb-position-rule-title">
  <div class="verb-rule">
    <div>
      <h2 id="verb-position-rule-title">Le verbe conjugué garde la place 2</h2>
      <p>
        Dans une <strong>proposition affirmative indépendante</strong>, le premier groupe peut changer. La forme
        verbale conjuguée reste le deuxième groupe.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div
      class="position-strip"
      aria-label="Structure d’une proposition affirmative indépendante"
      data-source-image-replacement="schéma de position du verbe"
    >
      <span>
        <small>Position 1</small>
        un groupe au choix
      </span>
      <span class="position-verb">
        <small>Position 2</small>
        verbe conjugué
      </span>
      <span>
        <small>Suite</small>
        autres groupes
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="verb-definition">
    Dans cette fiche, « verbe principal » désigne la <strong>forme verbale conjuguée avec le sujet</strong>,
    aussi appelée <strong>verbe fini</strong>.
  </p>

  <div class="syntax-role-legend" aria-label="Code couleur des exemples">
    <span><span class="role-chip mark-subject">sujet</span></span>
    <span><span class="role-chip mark-verb">verbe conjugué</span></span>
    <span><span class="role-chip mark-object">complément</span></span>
    <span><span class="role-chip mark-time">temps</span></span>
    <span><span class="role-chip mark-verbal-tail">forme finale</span></span>
  </div>

  <nav class="sentence-type-strip" aria-label="Place du verbe selon le type de phrase">
    {
      sentenceTypes.map((type) =>
        type.href ? (
          <a href={type.href}>
            <strong>{type.label}</strong>
            <span>{type.note}</span>
          </a>
        ) : (
          <span class="is-current">
            <strong>{type.label}</strong>
            <span>{type.note}</span>
          </span>
        ),
      )
    }
  </nav>

  <section class="position-demo" aria-labelledby="position-demo-title" data-position-demo>
    <div class="position-demo-heading">
      <div>
        <h3 id="position-demo-title">Change le premier groupe</h3>
        <p>Les quatre groupes restent les mêmes. Observe la position du verbe et du sujet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="position-demo-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Choisir le premier groupe">
      {
        examples.map((example, index) => (
          <button
            class:list={{ 'is-selected': index === 0 }}
            type="button"
            aria-controls={`position-example-${example.id}`}
            aria-pressed={index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
            data-position-choice={example.id}
          >
            {example.label}
          </button>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="position-demo-panels" aria-live="polite">
      <article id="position-example-subject" data-position-panel="subject">
        <p class="position-sentence" lang="de">
          <span class="mark-subject">Anna</span>
          <span class="mark-verb">liest</span>
          <span class="mark-time">heute</span>
          <span class="mark-object">dieses Buch</span>.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Anna</strong> prend la position 1 ; <strong>liest</strong> reste en position 2.</p>
      </article>

      <article id="position-example-time" data-position-panel="time" hidden>
        <p class="position-sentence" lang="de">
          <span class="mark-time">Heute</span>
          <span class="mark-verb">liest</span>
          <span class="mark-subject">Anna</span>
          <span class="mark-object">dieses Buch</span>.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Heute</strong> passe devant ; le sujet <strong>Anna</strong> se place après le verbe.</p>
      </article>

      <article id="position-example-object" data-position-panel="object" hidden>
        <p class="position-sentence" lang="de">
          <span class="mark-object">Dieses Buch</span>
          <span class="mark-verb">liest</span>
          <span class="mark-subject">Anna</span>
          <span class="mark-time">heute</span>.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Dieses Buch</strong> est mis en valeur ; le verbe reste le deuxième groupe.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="group-reminder" aria-label="Point important">
    <strong>2e position ne veut pas dire 2e mot.</strong>
    <span><span lang="de">Nach der Schule</span> forme un seul groupe et occupe toute la position 1.</span>
  </aside>

  <details class="lesson-card">
    <summary>Revoir les groupes d’une phrase</summary>
    <div class="lesson-card-content">
      <p>Une position accueille un groupe complet. Voici les cinq groupes à reconnaître en priorité.</p>
      <dl class="sentence-group-list">
        {
          sentenceGroups.map(([group, clue]) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{group}</dt>
              <dd>{clue}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </div>
  </details>

  <section class="two-form-content" aria-labelledby="two-form-title">
    <div>
      <h3 id="two-form-title">Quand la phrase contient deux formes verbales</h3>
      <p>Seule la forme conjuguée occupe la position 2. L’infinitif ou le participe passé ferme la phrase.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="two-form-list">
      <article>
        <strong>Passé composé</strong>
        <p lang="de">
          <span class="mark-subject">Anna</span>
          <span class="mark-verb">hat</span>
          <span class="mark-object">das Buch</span>
          <span class="mark-verbal-tail">gelesen</span>.
        </p>
        <small><span lang="de">hat</span> est conjugué ; <span lang="de">gelesen</span> reste à la fin.</small>
      </article>

      <article>
        <strong>Verbe de modalité</strong>
        <p lang="de">
          <span class="mark-subject">Anna</span>
          <span class="mark-verb">will</span>
          <span class="mark-object">das Buch</span>
          <span class="mark-verbal-tail">lesen</span>.
        </p>
        <small><span lang="de">will</span> est conjugué ; <span lang="de">lesen</span> reste à la fin.</small>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="related-links">
      Voir aussi :
      <a href={withBase('/theorie/syntaxe/les-phrases-au-passe-compose/')}>le passé composé</a>
      et
      <a href={withBase('/theorie/syntaxe/les-phrases-avec-verbe-de-modalite/')}>les verbes de modalité</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-position-demo]').forEach((demo) => {
    const buttons = Array.from(demo.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-position-choice]'));
    const panels = Array.from(demo.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-position-panel]'));

    buttons.forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const selectedId = button.dataset.positionChoice;

        buttons.forEach((choice) => {
          const isSelected = choice === button;
          choice.classList.toggle('is-selected', isSelected);
          choice.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(isSelected));
        });

        panels.forEach((panel) => {
          panel.hidden = panel.dataset.positionPanel !== selectedId;
        });
      });
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .syntax-lesson {
    display: grid;
    gap: 18px;
  }

  .verb-rule {
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
    padding: clamp(20px, 4vw, 30px);
    border: 2px solid rgba(169, 15, 47, 0.16);
    border-radius: 20px;
    background:
      linear-gradient(120deg, var(--grammar-verb-soft), transparent 44%),
      rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
  }

  .verb-rule h2,
  .position-demo h3 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .verb-rule p,
  .position-demo-heading p,
  .position-demo-panels p,
  .two-form-content p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .position-strip {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
  }

  .position-strip span {
    display: grid;
    min-height: 86px;
    align-content: center;
    gap: 4px;
    padding: 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 900;
  }

  .position-strip span + span {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .position-strip small {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .position-strip .position-verb {
    background: var(--grammar-verb-soft);
    color: var(--grammar-verb);
  }

  .verb-definition {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 15px;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--grammar-verb);
  }

  .syntax-role-legend {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .sentence-type-strip {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 9px;
  }

  .sentence-type-strip > a,
  .sentence-type-strip > span {
    display: grid;
    gap: 3px;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 12px;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 13px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .sentence-type-strip > a {
    transition:
      border-color 160ms ease,
      transform 160ms ease;
  }

  .sentence-type-strip > a:hover {
    border-color: rgba(169, 15, 47, 0.38);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  .sentence-type-strip > a:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--focus);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .sentence-type-strip .is-current {
    border-color: rgba(169, 15, 47, 0.26);
    background: var(--grammar-verb-soft);
  }

  .sentence-type-strip strong {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .sentence-type-strip span span,
  .sentence-type-strip a span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .position-demo {
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 2px solid rgba(31, 42, 68, 0.12);
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 0 rgba(15, 26, 49, 0.06);
  }

  .position-demo-heading {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
    padding: 20px 20px 14px;
  }

  .position-demo-buttons {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 0 20px 18px;
  }

  .position-demo-buttons button {
    min-height: 42px;
    padding: 9px 13px;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 11px;
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--ink);
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 850;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      border-color 160ms ease,
      background 160ms ease,
      transform 160ms ease;
  }

  .position-demo-buttons button:hover {
    border-color: rgba(169, 15, 47, 0.38);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  .position-demo-buttons button.is-selected {
    border-color: var(--grammar-verb);
    background: var(--grammar-verb-soft);
    color: var(--grammar-verb);
  }

  .position-demo-buttons button:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--focus);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .position-demo-panels {
    min-height: 150px;
    padding: clamp(20px, 4vw, 28px);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--border);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(246, 249, 255, 0.78), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96));
  }

  .position-demo-panels article[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .position-sentence {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(1.18rem, 3vw, 1.65rem);
    font-weight: 850;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .group-reminder {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-left: 5px solid var(--grammar-accusative);
    border-radius: 0 14px 14px 0;
    background: var(--grammar-accusative-soft);
  }

  .group-reminder strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .group-reminder span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .two-form-content {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: clamp(18px, 3vw, 24px);
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
  }

  .two-form-content h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .two-form-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .two-form-list article {
    padding: 14px;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.84);
  }

  .two-form-list article > p {
    margin: 8px 0 4px;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .two-form-list small {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .related-links {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .related-links a {
    color: var(--link);
    font-weight: 850;
  }

  .sentence-group-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .sentence-group-list > div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--surface-soft);
  }

  .sentence-group-list dt {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 900;
  }

  .sentence-group-list dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .position-strip,
    .sentence-type-strip,
    .sentence-group-list,
    .two-form-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .position-strip span + span {
      border-top: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-left: 0;
    }

  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .position-demo-buttons button,
    .sentence-type-strip > a {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
